  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full test suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nThe fix is one line in `src/click/core.py:392`. A child context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, the entry for its own name, instead of inheriting the parent's whole map.\n\nI added three tests to `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n- **Subcommand lookup:** `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": \"x\"}}` reaches the subcommand, and a top-level `{\"opt\": \"z\"}` does not leak into it.\n- **Nested groups:** `{\"grp\": {\"cmd\": {\"opt\": \"y\"}}}` reaches `cli \u2192 grp \u2192 cmd`.\n- **Precedence:** a `default_map` set in the subcommand's own `context_settings` still wins over the parent's.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
